# Kroll Automation — Client Brief

**Scope:** Build a Windows **automation application only** that drives the client’s existing **Kroll desktop app** (Telus). We do **not** build or replace Kroll. PoC (workflow engine, UIA automation, audit) is already complete.

**Team:** 2 developers, Cursor AI–assisted.

---

## 1. Technology stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Language | Python 3.11+ |
| Desktop automation | pywinauto (Microsoft UI Automation) |
| Agent UI | PyQt6 or system tray (pystray) |
| OCR | Tesseract / PaddleOCR (on-prem) or Azure Document Intelligence (cloud) |
| Data extraction | Regex/rules + optional Azure OpenAI |
| Workflow & validation | Existing workflow engine (PoC) |
| Audit & review queue | SQLite (single site) or PostgreSQL (multi-site) |
| Logs | JSON Lines (+ optional Sentry, no PHI in logs) |
| Installer | PyInstaller + Inno Setup (MSI) |
| Secrets | Windows Credential Manager / Azure Key Vault |
| CI / regression | GitHub Actions + PoC simulator |
| OS | Windows 10/11 (Kroll workstation) |

---

## 2. Architecture

```text
Incoming document (fax/email/PDF)
        ↓
   OCR + field extraction
        ↓
   Workflow engine (steps, verify, stop on fail)
        ↓
   Kroll UI adapter (pywinauto → real Kroll windows)
        ↓
   Kroll desktop app (installed by client)
        ↓
   Audit DB + human review queue (on failure)
```

**Components**

- **Automation agent** — tray/hotkey app; runs workflows on the pharmacist PC.
- **Kroll adapter** — finds controls by automation ID/name (not screen coordinates); read/set fields per tab.
- **Workflow engine** — Inbox → extract → Patient Search → Patient Record tabs → Save.
- **Verification** — after each field, read value back; mismatch → stop + screenshot + review queue.
- **PoC simulator** — regression testing only; not deployed to pharmacies.

**In-scope screens:** document intake, extraction review, Patient Search, Patient Record tabs (General, Insurance, Family, Allergies, Communications — ~20 fields per tab max), save/validation dialogs.

